    "body": "\nSix months ago: manual bid adjustments every Tuesday morning.\n\nToday: our Google & LinkedIn campaigns self-optimize while we focus on creative strategy.\n\nBut here's what nobody talks about—\n\nThe transition isn't just about turning on automated bidding.\n\nWe've audited 200+ accounts making this shift, and the ones that succeed follow a specific preparation sequence:\n\nWeek 1-2: Data foundation\nClean conversion tracking across both platforms. Google's Enhanced Conversions and LinkedIn's Conversion API need 30+ conversions per campaign to work properly.\n\nWeek 3-4: Portfolio consolidation  \nMerge similar campaign objectives into shared bid strategies. One Target CPA for lead gen across Google Search + LinkedIn Sponsored Content beats managing 12 individual campaigns.\n\nWeek 5-6: Creative volume ramp\nFeed the algorithms. Automated bidding needs 3-5 active ad variations per campaign to find winning combinations at scale.\n\nThe accounts that skip straight to \"set it and forget it\" see 40% higher CPAs in month one.\n\nThe ones that prep properly? They see 25% efficiency gains by month three.\n\nSmart automation isn't about doing less work. It's about doing different work.\n\nWhat's your experience been with transitioning to automated bidding? Any preparation steps we missed?\n"
